window.AG_PRACTICE = window.AG_PRACTICE || {};
window.AG_PRACTICE["bagang"] = {"id":"bagang","axis":"dx","seal":"診","scene":"art/scene-clinic.jpg","title":"Eight Principles","titleZh":"八綱辨證","sub":"Exterior/interior, cold/heat, deficiency/excess — and the two that contain them all","subZh":"表裡、寒熱、虛實，及統之者陰陽","mentor":{"key":"jing","nm":"Jìng Gū","nmZh":"靜姑","line":"\"Before you name a pattern, place it. Where is it, how hot is it, and is there something there or is something missing. Three questions. Everything else is detail.\"","lineZh":"「還沒給證取名之前，先把它放好。病在哪裡、冷還是熱、是多了什麼還是少了什麼。三問而已。其餘都是細節。」"},"card":{"h":"Three Questions, Then a Name 三問而後名","hZh":"","p":"Exterior or interior places the illness. Cold or heat gives it a temperature. Deficiency or excess says whether to build or to drain — and that single decision changes the needle technique, the moxa, and the whole formula.","pZh":"表裡以定其位，寒熱以定其性，虛實以定補瀉——而補瀉一決，手法、灸法、方藥皆隨之而變。"},"items":[{"k":"mc","q":"Which combination is the hallmark of an exterior pattern?","qZh":"表證之標誌為何？","opts":[{"t":"Chills and fever occurring together, with a floating pulse and a thin coat","c":"惡寒發熱並見，脈浮，苔薄","ok":1,"note":"The word is *together*. Once the chills stop and only heat remains, the pathogen has moved inside. Add a new onset, body aches and a stuffy nose and the exterior reading is secure. 要在「並見」二字。寒罷而熱獨存，則邪已入裡。更兼新起、身痛、鼻塞，其表證乃定。"},{"t":"Fever without chills, with a deep pulse","c":"但熱不寒，脈沉","ok":0,"note":"That is interior heat. Both findings point inward. 此為裡熱。二象俱指於裡。"},{"t":"Alternating chills and fever with a bitter mouth","c":"往來寒熱、口苦","ok":0,"note":"That is half exterior, half interior — the Shaoyang pattern, which has its own treatment. 此為半表半裡之少陽證，別有治法。"},{"t":"Aversion to cold that improves with warmth, over many months","c":"畏寒得溫則減，歷月而成","ok":0,"note":"Aversion to cold relieved by warmth over months is interior yang deficiency 畏寒, not the exterior chill 惡寒 that no amount of blankets fixes. The distinction is one of the most useful in the whole system. 畏寒者得溫則減，屬裡陽虛；惡寒者雖厚衣重被而不解，屬表。此辨最為切用。"}]},{"k":"match","q":"Match each finding to the principle it decides.","qZh":"症象配所決之綱。","pairs":[{"l":"Floating pulse, chills with fever","lZh":"脈浮、惡寒發熱","r":"Exterior","rZh":"表"},{"l":"Thirst for cold drinks, dark urine, red tongue","lZh":"渴喜冷飲、尿黃、舌紅","r":"Heat","rZh":"熱"},{"l":"Pain relieved by pressure, weak pulse, long illness","lZh":"痛喜按、脈弱、病久","r":"Deficiency","rZh":"虛"},{"l":"Pain worse with pressure, forceful pulse, sudden onset","lZh":"痛拒按、脈有力、新起","r":"Excess","rZh":"實"},{"l":"Clear copious urine, loose stool, pale wet tongue","lZh":"小便清長、便溏、舌淡潤","r":"Cold","rZh":"寒"}],"note":"Notice how each principle has a *cluster* behind it, never one finding. One sign can lie; four signs pointing the same way rarely do. 每綱之後皆有一組症象，不憑一症。一症可欺，四症同指則罕誤。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which pair of findings separates deficiency from excess most reliably?","qZh":"辨虛實，何二象最可憑？","opts":[{"t":"Whether pressure relieves or aggravates, and whether the pulse has force","c":"喜按拒按，與脈之有力無力","ok":1,"note":"Emptiness welcomes support: pressure comforts, warmth comforts, and the pulse is soft. Fullness resists: pressure hurts, the pulse pushes back. These two questions cost nothing and settle the treatment principle. 虛則喜其助：按之則舒，得溫則減，脈亦軟。實則拒之：按之則痛，脈亦有力。此二問不費一物，而補瀉之則已定。"},{"t":"The patient's age and how thin they are","c":"年歲與形之肥瘦","ok":0,"note":"Both are worth noting as background, but a thin young person can hold a full pathogen and a stout older one can be profoundly empty. 二者可為參考，然瘦弱者可挾實邪，肥壯者亦可大虛。"},{"t":"Whether the illness started in winter","c":"是否起於冬令","ok":0,"note":"Season shapes which pathogen is likely, not whether the pattern is empty or full. 時令示邪之所偏，不決虛實。"},{"t":"Whether the tongue has a coating","c":"舌之有苔無苔","ok":0,"note":"Useful, and it does lean — a stripped coat suggests depletion — but on its own it is far weaker than pressure and pulse force. 有所偏助，苔剝提示虧損；然獨憑此象，遠不如按與脈之可據。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A patient is flushed, restless and thirsty, yet wants hot drinks, has clear urine and a deep weak pulse. What is happening?","qZh":"面赤煩躁而渴，然喜熱飲、小便清、脈沉無力。此何謂？","opts":[{"t":"True cold with false heat","c":"真寒假熱","ok":1,"note":"When yang is exhausted it can be forced outward, producing a convincing surface of heat over a cold interior. The tell is always the *deep* findings: what the patient drinks, what the urine looks like, and the pulse under pressure. Treat the true cold, not the false heat. This is a serious presentation and belongs with a qualified practitioner. 陽衰而格於外，故外見假熱而內實真寒。其憑常在深處：所飲之寒溫、小便之清濁、沉取之脈勢。當治其真寒，不治其假熱。此證非輕，宜由有資格之醫者處理。"},{"t":"True heat with false cold","c":"真熱假寒","ok":0,"note":"That is the mirror image: cold limbs on the outside but thirst for cold drinks, dark urine, foul stool and a forceful deep pulse. 此其鏡像：外見肢冷，而渴喜冷飲、小便黃赤、大便臭穢、脈沉而有力。"},{"t":"Straightforward excess heat","c":"純為實熱","ok":0,"note":"Excess heat wants cold drinks and produces dark urine and a forceful pulse. Two of the three contradict here. 實熱者喜冷飲、尿黃赤、脈有力。本案三者中二者相違。"},{"t":"Exterior wind-heat","c":"風熱表證","ok":0,"note":"Exterior patterns are new, float, and come with chills. This pulse is deep and weak. 表證新起、脈浮、兼惡寒。本案脈沉而無力。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which statement about yin and yang in the Eight Principles is correct?","qZh":"八綱之中，陰陽二綱，何說為是？","opts":[{"t":"They are the summary of the other six","c":"陰陽為六綱之總","ok":1,"note":"Exterior, heat and excess group under yang; interior, cold and deficiency group under yin. This is why the very first line of a case write-up can be a single word — and why yin-yang is called the great guideline 總綱. 表、熱、實統於陽；裡、寒、虛統於陰。故案首一字可定其大體，而陰陽稱為總綱。"},{"t":"They are a ninth and tenth principle used only in severe cases","c":"為第九第十綱，惟重證用之","ok":0,"note":"They are not additional — they contain the rest. 陰陽非別立，乃統攝其餘。"},{"t":"They apply only to the pulse","c":"專指脈象","ok":0,"note":"They apply to every level of the diagnosis. 陰陽貫於辨證之各層。"},{"t":"Yang means the patient is strong","c":"陽即謂其人壯","ok":0,"note":"Yang describes the pattern, not the constitution. A frail patient can present a yang pattern. 陽言其證，不言其體。羸弱者亦可見陽證。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Which presentation is a MIXED pattern rather than a single one?","qZh":"下列何者為相兼之證，而非單一之證？","opts":[{"t":"Chills and fever with body aches, together with long-standing fatigue and loose stool","c":"惡寒發熱身痛，兼素體倦怠便溏","ok":1,"note":"An exterior pathogen on a deficient base — extremely common and easy to mishandle. Drain hard and you exhaust the patient; tonify only and you trap the pathogen inside. Usually you release the exterior while supporting the base. 表邪而兼裡虛，臨床極常見，最易誤治。專事攻邪則傷其正，專事扶正則閉門留寇。多以解表兼扶正為法。"},{"t":"Fever, thirst, dark urine and a forceful rapid pulse","c":"發熱、口渴、尿赤、脈數有力","ok":0,"note":"A clean interior excess heat pattern. Every finding agrees. 純為裡實熱，諸象一致。"},{"t":"Chills, no sweating, thin white coat, floating tight pulse","c":"惡寒無汗、苔薄白、脈浮緊","ok":0,"note":"A clean exterior wind-cold pattern. 純為風寒表實。"},{"t":"Fatigue, breathlessness, spontaneous sweating, weak pulse","c":"倦怠、氣短、自汗、脈弱","ok":0,"note":"A clean qi deficiency pattern. 純為氣虛。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Why does deciding deficiency versus excess matter more than naming the organ?","qZh":"何以辨虛實較定臟腑更為要緊？","opts":[{"t":"Because it decides whether to build or to drain, and getting it backwards makes the patient worse","c":"以其決補瀉。補瀉一反，病必加重","ok":1,"note":"Naming the wrong organ usually makes a treatment less effective. Reversing deficiency and excess makes it actively harmful — draining an empty patient, or tonifying while a pathogen is still lodged 閉門留寇. This is why the excess-deficiency question comes early in every case in this game. 誤定其臟，多不過效減。虛實一反，則為害：虛而瀉之則奪其正，邪未去而補之則閉門留寇。故本遊戲諸案，虛實之問恆在其先。"},{"t":"Because organs are not important in TCM","c":"以中醫不重臟腑","ok":0,"note":"Organs are central. The point is one of order: place the pattern first, then locate it. 臟腑至要。所言者次第耳：先定其性，後定其位。"},{"t":"Because the pulse cannot show the organ","c":"以脈不能候臟","ok":0,"note":"The three positions do reflect the organs. That is not the reason. 三部本候臟腑，非其故也。"},{"t":"Because excess patterns are always more serious","c":"以實證恆重於虛證","ok":0,"note":"Not so — a profound deficiency can be far more serious than a brisk excess. 未必。大虛之候，常較新實為重。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"A long illness that suddenly turns acute and forceful. How should the Eight Principles handle this?","qZh":"久病而忽轉急重有力，八綱當如何看？","opts":[{"t":"Read it as an excess arising on a deficient base, and treat the urgent part first","c":"作虛中夾實觀，急則治其標","ok":1,"note":"The eight principles are not permanent labels — they describe a moment. Patterns transform: cold turns to heat, exterior moves interior, excess exhausts into deficiency. The classical rule is that the urgent branch is treated first, the root afterwards. 八綱非固定之標籤，乃一時之象。證能轉化：寒可化熱，表可入裡，實久而致虛。古法：急則治其標，緩則治其本。"},{"t":"Ignore the new findings, since the old pattern is the true one","c":"棄其新見，仍守舊證","ok":0,"note":"The patient in front of you today is the case. Yesterday's pattern is history, not evidence. 所診者今日之人。昨日之證為記錄，非憑據。"},{"t":"Conclude the earlier diagnosis was wrong","c":"斷前診為誤","ok":0,"note":"Possible, but transformation is at least as likely and much commoner. Re-examine before concluding. 或有之，然轉化之機更為常見。當復診而後斷。"},{"t":"Treat the root only and wait","c":"專治其本而待之","ok":0,"note":"When the branch is urgent, waiting is a decision with consequences. 標急而待，其待亦有其果。"}]},{"k":"order","q":"Put the three questions in the order they are usually asked.","qZh":"排出辨證三問之常序。","seq":[{"t":"Exterior or interior?","c":"表裡？"},{"t":"Cold or heat?","c":"寒熱？"},{"t":"Deficiency or excess?","c":"虛實？"}],"note":"Location, then temperature, then whether to build or drain. Some cases invert the first two — a chronic interior case may settle location instantly — but this is the order that rescues you when a case is confusing. 先定位，次定性，末定補瀉。慢性裡證或可即定其位而先問寒熱；然遇疑難之案，此序最可倚。"},{"k":"mc","q":"Which of these is a red flag that should send a patient for conventional medical assessment rather than into a training exercise?","qZh":"何者為紅旗症狀，當令病人就正規醫療評估，而非留於練習？","opts":[{"t":"Sudden severe headache unlike any before, with vomiting and confusion","c":"驟起劇烈頭痛，前所未有，兼嘔吐、神志不清","ok":1,"note":"Sudden, severe, and unlike anything before — with vomiting or altered awareness — needs urgent conventional assessment, not pattern differentiation. Recognising the limits of the frame is part of competence, not a failure of it. Other red flags: chest pain with breathlessness, sudden one-sided weakness or speech loss, unexplained weight loss, blood where it should not be, and any fever with a stiff neck. 驟起、劇烈、前所未有，兼嘔吐或神志改變者，當急送正規醫療，非辨證之時。知其界限，正屬醫者之能，非其短。他如胸痛兼氣促、驟然偏身無力或言語不能、不明原因之體重驟減、異常出血、發熱兼項強，皆同。"},{"t":"A dull headache before the menstrual period each month","c":"經前頭痛隱隱，按月而作","ok":0,"note":"A recognisable pattern worth differentiating in clinic. 此為可辨之證，宜於臨床細分。"},{"t":"A headache at the temples after a stressful week","c":"勞心一週而兩顳作痛","ok":0,"note":"Ordinary, and often a Liver pattern. 常見，多屬肝。"},{"t":"A heavy, muzzy head in damp weather","c":"陰雨則頭重如裹","ok":0,"note":"A classic damp presentation. 濕證之典型。"}]},{"k":"mc","q":"Interior heat and exterior cold in the same patient. Is this possible?","qZh":"表寒而裡熱並見，可乎？","opts":[{"t":"Yes — the principles describe different axes and can combine","c":"可 — 諸綱各為一軸，故可相兼","ok":1,"note":"Exterior-interior is location and cold-heat is temperature; they are independent, so all combinations exist. Exterior cold with interior heat is common enough to have its own classical treatment approach — release the exterior and clear the interior at the same time. 表裡言其位，寒熱言其性，二軸各自獨立，故諸合皆有。表寒裡熱者，古已有法：解表與清裡並行。"},{"t":"No — a patient can only be in one place at a time","c":"不可 — 病不能同時在二處","ok":0,"note":"A pathogen on the surface and a pre-existing interior heat coexist routinely. 邪在表而裡本有熱，二者並存，臨床常見。"},{"t":"No — cold and heat cancel out","c":"不可 — 寒熱相消","ok":0,"note":"They coexist in different locations rather than cancelling. Upper heat with lower cold 上熱下寒 is another familiar example. 二者分居異位而並存，非相消。上熱下寒即其一例。"},{"t":"Only in children","c":"惟小兒有之","ok":0,"note":"It occurs at any age. 各年齡皆有。"}]}]};
